00:04:13,548 --> 00:04:19,548
Hell, any of them could have done it.

2
00:08:27,096 --> 00:08:33,096
Knives Out is a comedy, crime, mystery film directed by Rian Johnson.

3
00:12:40,645 --> 00:12:46,645
When renowned crime novelist Harlan Thrombey is found dead at his estate just after his 85th birthday, the
inquisitive and debonair Detective Benoit Blanc is mysteriously enlisted to investigate.

4
00:16:54,193 --> 00:17:00,193
From Harlan's dysfunctional family to his devoted staff, Blanc sifts through a web of red
herrings and self-serving lies to uncover the truth behind Harlan's untimely death.

5
00:21:07,741 --> 00:21:13,741
Benoit Blanc, played by Daniel Craig.

6
00:25:21,290 --> 00:25:27,290
Ransom Drysdale, played by Chris Evans.

7
00:29:34,838 --> 00:29:40,838
Marta Cabrera, played by Ana de Armas.

8
00:33:48,387 --> 00:33:54,387
Linda Drysdale, played by Jamie Lee Curtis.

9
00:38:01,935 --> 00:38:07,935
Walt Thrombey, played by Michael Shannon.

10
00:42:15,483 --> 00:42:21,483
Richard Drysdale, played by Don Johnson.

11
00:46:29,032 --> 00:46:35,032
Knives Out is a 2019 American mystery film written and directed by Rian Johnson.

12
00:50:42,580 --> 00:50:48,580
The film's eleven-actor ensemble cast is led by Daniel Craig as Benoit Blanc, a famed private detective
who is summoned to investigate the death of a bestselling author (Christopher Plummer).

13
00:54:56,129 --> 00:55:02,129
Police think his death is a suicide but Blanc suspects foul play
and investigates to ascertain the true cause of it.

14
00:59:09,677 --> 00:59:15,677
Johnson produced Knives Out with his longtime collaborator Ram Bergman.

15
01:03:23,225 --> 01:03:29,225
Funding came from MRC and tax subsidies from the Massachusetts state government.

16
01:07:36,774 --> 01:07:42,774
Johnson conceived Knives Out in the mid-2000s.

17
01:11:50,322 --> 01:11:56,322
Wanting to create work reminiscent of whodunit films of the mid-twentieth century, the director
was influenced by his interest in movie adaptations of Agatha Christie's stories.

18
01:16:03,870 --> 01:16:09,870
Development of Knives Out continued after Johnson finished
filming Star Wars: The Last Jedi (2017).

19
01:20:17,419 --> 01:20:23,419
He wrote the screenplay in six to seven months.

20
01:24:30,967 --> 01:24:36,967
Principal photography on Knives Out began in October 2018 on a
$40 million budget and ended that December.

21
01:28:44,516 --> 01:28:50,516
Location filming took place in suburban Boston.

22
01:32:58,064 --> 01:33:04,064
Nathan Johnson composed the film's classical score, which was
inspired by his and Rian's favorite symphonic movie scores.

23
01:37:11,612 --> 01:37:17,612
Knives Out has been read as a work that investigates class warfare, wealth
inequality, immigration, and race in contemporary American society.

24
01:41:25,161 --> 01:41:31,161
Knives Out premiered at the 44th Toronto International Film Festival on September 7,
2019, and was distributed by Lionsgate to American theaters on November 27.

25
01:45:38,709 --> 01:45:44,709
The film was a critical and commercial success; the National Board of Review and the American Film
Institute chose it as one of the year's top films, and it grossed $312 million.

26
01:49:52,258 --> 01:49:58,258
Knives Out received highly positive reviews from critics, who praised the plot and
actors but occasionally criticized aspects of the writing and performances.

27
01:54:05,806 --> 01:54:11,806
It was nominated for multiple awards, including three Golden Globes, a British
Academy Film Award, and an Academy Award for Best Original Screenplay.

28
01:58:19,354 --> 01:58:25,354
Knives Out is the first entry of a series of films that also
includes Glass Onion (2022) and Wake Up Dead Man (2025).

29
02:02:32,903 --> 02:02:38,903
The film explores themes of immigrant, detective,
massachusetts, investigation, big family.

30
02:06:46,451 --> 02:06:52,451
The tone is lighthearted and dark and mind_bending.
